{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-41557",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we decompose all of the terms into their various factors. The $32x(5z+1)$ in the numerator becomes $2\\cdot 2\\cdot 2\\cdot 2\\cdot 2\\cdot x\\cdot (5z+1),$ and the $12xz$ in the denominator becomes $3\\cdot 2\\cdot 2\\cdot x\\cdot z.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{32x(5z+1)}{12xz}=\\frac{2\\cdot 2\\cdot 2\\cdot 2\\cdot 2\\cdot x\\cdot (5z+1)}{3\\cdot 2\\cdot 2\\cdot x\\cdot z}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we cancel out all the pairs of common factors in the numerator and denominator. In this case, there are two pairs of $2\\text{'s}$ and one pair of $x$'s.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2\\cdot 2\\cdot 2\\cdot 2\\cdot 2\\cdot x\\cdot (5z+1)}{3\\cdot 2\\cdot 2\\cdot x\\cdot z} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{2}\\cdot \\cancel{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2\\cdot 2\\cdot \\cancel{x}\\cdot (5z+1)}{3\\cdot \\cancel{2}\\cdot \\cancel{2}\\cdot \\cancel{x}\\cdot z} & = \\\\ \\frac{2\\cdot 2\\cdot 2\\cdot (5z+1)}{3\\cdot z} & = \\\\ \\frac{8(5z+1)}{3z}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the expression simplifies to $\\frac{8(5z+1)}{3z}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
